      "text": "Hacienda Venecia Coffee Plantation"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c806fc2e6cfa0e7c8f3e02c5042eb5417f56d9d1fbd2aed70d16a868d5b04147",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-chat-202611100526-00e424b1aafd",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast. Transfer to Hacienda Venecia.\n\nYour introduction to Colombian coffee begins with a freshly brewed cup. Then you'll learn about the origins and history of coffee, its varieties, and what distinguishes different grades of coffee.\n\nOn a walk through the plantation, you'll follow the beans from cultivation and harvesting through cleaning and sorting to the finished cup. You can take part in some of these steps yourself.\n\nAfter the main part of the tour, you'll have a traditional Colombian lunch.\n\nAfter lunch, a workshop introduces different ways to brew coffee. Compare the aroma and flavor each method brings out and learn what sets familiar brewing methods apart.\n\nAt the end of the tour, transfer to the hotel. Time to relax."
    },
